"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"interruptedRunId\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"generation\""},{"type":"text","value":">\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Omit"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResponseSchemaInterruptBindingBase"},{"type":"text","value":" & "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"interruptedRunId\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"generation\""},{"type":"text","value":">\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Omit"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterruptBindingBase"},{"type":"text","value":" & "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"interruptedRunId\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"generation\""},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Interrupt"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"descriptor","text":"descriptor","level":3},{"id":"binding","text":"binding","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction withInterruptBinding(descriptor, binding): Interrupt;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/interrupt-resume.ts:954](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/interrupt-resume.ts#L954)\n\nAttach a resume binding to an interrupt descriptor, under\n[INTERRUPT\\_BINDING\\_METADATA\\_KEY](../variables/INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY.md).\n\nThis is the supported way to make an interrupt resumable by this package.\nThe descriptor keeps its AG-UI shape; only `metadata` gains the namespaced\nkey. Pass the unopened form (no `interruptedRunId` / `generation`) when\nemitting from inside a run — those fields are stamped as the run finishes.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### descriptor\n\n`Interrupt`\n\n### binding\n\n  \\| [`InterruptBinding`](../type-aliases/InterruptBinding.md)\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`ResponseSchemaInterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`ResponseSchemaInterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`InterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n`Interrupt`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: withInterruptBinding\ntitle: withInterruptBinding\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction withInterruptBinding(descriptor, binding): Interrupt;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/interrupt-resume.ts:954](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/interrupt-resume.ts#L954)\n\nAttach a resume binding to an interrupt descriptor, under\n[INTERRUPT\\_BINDING\\_METADATA\\_KEY](../variables/INTERRUPT_BINDING_METADATA_KEY.md).\n\nThis is the supported way to make an interrupt resumable by this package.\nThe descriptor keeps its AG-UI shape; only `metadata` gains the namespaced\nkey. Pass the unopened form (no `interruptedRunId` / `generation`) when\nemitting from inside a run — those fields are stamped as the run finishes.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### descriptor\n\n`Interrupt`\n\n### binding\n\n  \\| [`InterruptBinding`](../type-aliases/InterruptBinding.md)\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`ResponseSchemaInterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`ResponseSchemaInterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n  \\| `Omit`\\<`InterruptBindingBase` & `object`, `\"interruptedRunId\"` \\| `\"generation\"`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n`Interrupt`\n"}
